<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nikephoros II Orsini</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1328–<a href="/years/1359">1359</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Nikephoros II of Epirus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nikephoros II Orsini was the last Orsini ruler of the Despotate of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a>, reigning from 1335 to 1340 and again from 1356 to 1359. His first reign ended when the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> annexed Epirus, and in 1356 he regained part of it from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> after the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stefan-dusan">Stefan Dušan</a>. He was killed in 1359 fighting Albanian clans near the Achelous river, after which they divided southern Epirus.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nikephoros-ii-orsini.jpg" alt="Nikephoros II Orsini" width="320" height="302" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Epir1315-1358.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
